msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:53
msgid "Open the ``15-Bluetooth_remote_relay.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\bluetooth\\15-Bluetooth_remote_relay``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:55
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:57
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. You should read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:65
msgid "If you read ``[!] no reply from the module``, the module is not answering on D0/D1 - check the four wires and the power supply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:70
msgid "3. Switch It from the Phone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:72
msgid "Open LightBlue, tap **Scan** and connect to **SunFounder-C2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:74
msgid "Expand the service **0xA002** and open the characteristic **C304**. Then tap **Write new value**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:79
msgid "Set the format in the top right corner to **UTF-8 String** and type ``1``. The picture shows the field just before sending:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:84
msgid "Send it. The relay clicks, its indicator LED lights up and the Serial Monitor prints ``On``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:87
msgid "Type ``0`` in the same field and send it - the relay clicks back and the monitor prints ``Off``. The picture shows the field again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:95
msgid "Some relay modules work the other way round: they switch on when the pin is **LOW**. If yours clicks the opposite way, swap ``HIGH`` and ``LOW`` in the sketch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:100
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:102
msgid "**One pin, one switch**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:111
msgid "Writing ``LOW`` in ``setup()`` matters: a pin that has just become an output may start HIGH for a moment and make the relay click every time the board resets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:114
msgid "**The command check**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:126
msgid "Same shape as the lock project: the state comes from the phone, and anything that is not ``1`` or ``0`` is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:129
msgid "**Why the relay is not driven directly from the phone**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/15-iot_Bluetooth_remote_relay.rst:131
msgid "The phone talks to the module, the module talks to the board over two wires, and the board drives the relay. Each step only passes a short command along - that is why a single character is enough even though three devices are involved."
msgstr ""
